misc: fastrpc: let the freezer park a waiting invoke

An invoke interrupted by the freezer returns -ERESTARTSYS and is restarted
after thaw as a new message. hexagonrpcd's listener is always blocked in
one, so every system suspend sent the sensor DSP a second copy of its
pending call, and the DSP crashed 6 ms after tasks restarted
(EX:sensor_process:0x1:frpc_dsp:0x6c). With TASK_FREEZABLE the freezer
freezes the sleeping caller in place, and a completion that arrives
meanwhile is kept for the thaw.

--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1182,7 +1182,15 @@
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/*
+		 * Freezable, so that system suspend parks a waiting caller
+		 * instead of interrupting it. An interrupted invoke is
+		 * restarted as a second message for the same call, and the
+		 * sensor DSP crashes on it (EX:sensor_process:frpc_dsp) as
+		 * soon as tasks are thawed.
+		 */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	if (err)
